---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { COMPANY, getApp } from '../../data/apps';

const app = getApp('sortie')!;
const updatedDate = 'August 22, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`${app.name} Support - ${COMPANY.name}`}
  description="Help with the iPhone-only Sortie pre-release build, local campaign saves, and optional Apple Game Center achievements."
  path="/sortie/support"
  noindex={true}
  socialImage="/apps/sortie.png"
  socialImageAlt="Sortie app icon"
>
  <article class="prose container">
    <a class="back-link" href="/sortie">&larr; {app.name}</a>
    <h1>{app.name} Support</h1>
    <p class="updated">Updated: {updatedDate}</p>

    <p class="callout">
      <strong>Current availability.</strong> {app.name} is an iPhone-only,
      portrait pre-release build for iOS 14 or later. It is not supported on
      iPad, and there is no public App Store listing, public TestFlight
      acquisition link, or announced price.
    </p>

    <h2>Get direct help</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.email}`}>{COMPANY.email}</a> with the
      iPhone model, iOS version, {app.name} version or build number, affected
      level, and the steps that led to the problem. Include a screenshot only
      if you are comfortable sharing what it contains.
    </p>
    <p>
      Do not send your Apple Account password, verification codes, payment
      information, or other credentials.
    </p>

    <h2>If Sortie will not launch</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Confirm the device is an iPhone running iOS 14 or later.</li>
      <li>Install the newest authorized pre-release build available to you.</li>
      <li>Hold the iPhone in portrait orientation and reopen {app.name}.</li>
      <li>Restart the iPhone and confirm it has available storage.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      Avoid deleting {app.name} as an early troubleshooting step if the iPhone
      may contain the only local copy of campaign progress you want to keep.
    </p>

    <h2>Local campaign progress</h2>
    <p>
      {app.name} stores completed campaign progress, level records, wins, best
      times, and settings in a local JSON save inside the app's container. It
      has no Nintek account, cloud-save service, or gameplay backend.
      {COMPANY.name} cannot retrieve or rebuild that local save from a server.
    </p>
    <p>
      If progress or a record looks wrong, do not delete or reinstall the app.
      Note the last completed level you remember, whether the problem followed
      an update, and what changed, then include those details when contacting
      support.
    </p>

    <h2>Optional Game Center achievements</h2>
    <p>
      The full 1,500-level campaign works without Game Center. To report
      achievements, confirm Game Center is enabled and signed in under Apple
      Settings, connect the iPhone to the internet, and reopen {app.name}. The
      current integration reports achievements only; it does not use
      leaderboards.
    </p>
    <p>
      Apple controls Game Center authentication, player profiles, and
      achievement records. {COMPANY.name} cannot reset a Game Center profile,
      change an Apple Account, or delete Apple-held records.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="https://support.apple.com/guide/iphone/set-up-your-game-center-profile-iphd26b2beaa/ios">
        Apple: set up and manage a Game Center profile
      </a>
    </p>

    <h2>Deleting or reinstalling Sortie</h2>
    <p>
      Deleting {app.name} removes its local save from that iPhone. The data
      cannot be recovered from a Nintek server. Apple-managed device backups
      may behave according to your Apple backup settings, while Game Center
      achievements remain associated with Apple's service.
    </p>

    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Read the <a href="/sortie/privacy/">Sortie Privacy Policy</a> for details
      about local storage, Apple-managed backups, optional Game Center,
      tracking, retention, and deletion.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
